2. Copies a payload into that memory
3. Starts a new thread pointing at the payload
4. Waits for the thread to finish

**Important:** This is a dual‑use technique commonly used in malware and red‑team tooling. Only compile and run it on systems you own or have explicit written authorization to test. Most AV/EDR products will flag executable memory allocation + new thread execution.

